      "problem": "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $h$ maps the interval from $0$ to $1$ exclusive to the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $1$ only.\"*",
      "worked_solution": "The sentence *\"The function $h$ maps the interval from $0$ to $1$ exclusive to the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $1$ only\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $h:(0,1)\\to \\{0,1\\}$\n\nHere, the domain of $h$ is $(0,1),$ and the codomain of $h$ is $\\{0,1\\}.$",
